      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I suspect that it is probably caused when this bug occurs.\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/overlapping-menus\nAlso, a bit off-topic, but there was certainly a case that I was in desktop mode and pressing ESC did not (strictly) cancel drop mode in build 1238. (But I think this is probably not depending on the mentioned bug, and I cannot reproduce it now.)\nIn this case, ESC must be pressed twice to cancel the drop mode (i.e., close the menu).\nThis allowed me to move to another instance while in drop mode, and immediately after the move, I would get an error message like \"Cannot place portal\".\nEDIT: It seems that the portal is ready to be placed in an unknown space. I did not get an error message (the correct one was \"Could not find surfaces~\") immediately after the move.",
